    "answer": {
      "short": "$36$.",
      "worked": "Try digit pairs and compare twice their product with the two-digit number they form. For digits $3$ and $6$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\times6&=18\\\\2\\times(3\\times6)&=2\\times18\\\\2\\times(3\\times6)&=36\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe digits of $36$ are $3$ and $6$, so $36$ satisfies the condition.",
